Z||000010||FieroSTETZ||10-29-2000||12:18 AM||||i was actually going about 60. my brother and I have made quite a few films, and have learned some camera tricks. the chase car was going fairly slow, and the camera was set to focus on the sidewalk, not on my car, makes it blur the car and look faster. the main reason for the video being as choppy as it is is so you can hear my cool engine noise. at the time, I did not have a flowmaster and 3" tubing, so i think its time for another round with the camera (and my new software! haven't forgotten, i have to find it again- messy data backup- gotta sort through roughly 35gb on my server) and my car has the following mods:<BR>-175 deg. thermostat<BR>-quick release alternator/accessory belt retainer<BR>-aftermarket cam (Don't know, installed at speed shop by prior owner)<BR>-flowmaster series 40<BR>-all extra weight removed<BR>and other stuff which i can't remember right now (just worked 14 hours, inventory time at comp USA, woohoo...)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460599&p=25516673"> ||||reg||1
